    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-005",
      "title": "Past simple of frequent regular and irregular verbs",
      "explanation": "Use the past simple for finished actions with a time word like yesterday. Regular verbs add -ed (play, played; work, worked; watch, watched). Spelling changes: study becomes studied; stop becomes stopped. Irregular verbs have their own forms and must be learned: go, went; have, had; see, saw; eat, ate; buy, bought; make, made. The past form is the same for all persons: I went, she went, they went.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I played football yesterday."
        },
        {
          "en": "She went to the market."
        },
        {
          "en": "We ate pizza."
        }
      ],
