    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-008",
      "title": "Negative statements with be and do",
      "explanation": "With be, add not after the verb: I am not tired. He isn't at home. They aren't here. With other verbs in the present simple, use don't (do not) or doesn't (does not) before the base verb: They don't live here. She doesn't like coffee. The main verb does not take -s after doesn't. Both the full and the contracted forms are correct.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I am not tired."
        },
        {
          "en": "She doesn't like coffee."
        },
        {
          "en": "They don't live here."
        }
      ],
